&ÍŸ¶ºx£Zrœ∫£-ÍoMÒ’=µiVÍÇ0ß≈«µ|{"url":"/gcsl/working-with-files/workspaces/","fragment":{"page_number":0,"data":{"url":"/gcsl/working-with-files/workspaces/","content":"Workspaces. A GCSL workspace is a directory tree rooted at workspace.gcsl. Files in one directory share public declarations. Child directories inherit the public declarations above them, so common types and helpers can live at the root without repeated imports. The marker is an ordinary GCSL source file. It can be empty or declare shared values and functions. The disk loader finds the nearest enclosing marker when you run a file, reads the workspace, and checks every source before executing the selected file and its dependencies. Public and private names # Fields, def functions, and declared types contribute to a directory's public scope. let, let mut, and fn bindings remain private to their file. Dotted public paths merge when they define distinct leaves; a conflicting leaf is an error unless an earlier declaration explicitly permits shadowing. Sibling and child directories are not automatically in scope. Imports name paths from the workspace root, with / between directories, as the file system does. import lib/helpers names lib/helpers.gcsl or a directory of that path. Use as for a local alias, or import a named member with from. A directory or file name in a path is written as it is, dots and all, so import pkgs/net.busybox.busybox as busybox names the directory pkgs/net.busybox.busybox. An import without as is named after the path's last part, so that part must be a plain name; give a name such as net.busybox.busybox one with as. Boundaries and evaluation order # Hidden names and nested directories containing their own workspace.gcsl are excluded from an enclosing workspace's source discovery. A nested workspace is independent, not an importable child module of the outer workspace. Symbolic-link directory traversal is not a mechanism for extending the source tree. Dependencies determine file order; path order breaks ties. A file runs as a whole before a file that depends on it. Cyclic file dependencies are errors, including cycles introduced through function bodies or imports. A standalone file outside any workspace can import standard modules but cannot import arbitrary neighboring source files. Create a workspace marker when several files need to cooperate. Deliberate overrides # #[shadowable] marks a public declaration or import as replaceable by a later declaration in the workspace's defined order. The implicit prelude import is shadowable, so your own declarations can use its names. Use this attribute for intentional defaults. It is not an escape from all conflicts: an ordinary public leaf still cannot be defined twice. Whole-value overrides replace the old value, while distinct dotted leaves can merge. See gcsl(5) for ordering and import syntax.","word_count":422,"filters":{},"meta":{"crumbs":"GCSL / Files and Workspaces","title":"Workspaces"},"anchors":[{"element":"h2","id":"public-and-private-names","text":"Public and private names #","location":85},{"element":"h2","id":"boundaries-and-evaluation-order","text":"Boundaries and evaluation order #","location":236},{"element":"h2","id":"deliberate-overrides","text":"Deliberate overrides #","location":345}]}},"word_data":{"symbol":[{"position":272,"weight":12,"original_word":null}],"link":[{"position":272,"weight":12,"original_word":null}],"escap":[{"position":390,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"still":[{"position":398,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"check":[{"position":74,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"their":[{"position":111,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":247,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"conflict":[{"position":123,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":393,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"need":[{"position":342,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"gcsl5":[{"position":416,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"introduc":[{"position":312,"weight":24,"original_wor